==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|ends up|ending up|ended up|ended up}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic; with the preposition [[with]]}} To [[conclude]], [[turn out]], sometimes unexpectedly.
#: ''How did things '''end up''' with you and the bricklayer?'' &mdash; ''Great. We got married!''
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[arrive]] at a destination, sometimes unexpectedly.
#: ''I was going for a stroll, and '''ended up''' in Slovakia.''
# {{lb|en|of a set of events}} To [[eventually]] [[do]]
#: ''We spent a long time looking for a cheaper deal, but we '''ended up''' buying from the first dealer we met.''
# To lift or tilt, so as to set on end.
#: ''to '''end up''' a hogshead''

